# State and event model

Hand-edited diagrams of the three case-type state machines, as implemented in `CaseState`, `BatchCaseState`, `ExceptionCaseState` and the `*Configuration` event handlers.

Edit the Mermaid in this file (`tech_docs/source/state-event-model.html.md.erb`). Business writes for each event stay in [CCD architecture — States and events](/ccd-architecture.html#states-and-events). Who can see an event in ExUI stays in the [Next step events matrix](/next-step-events-matrix.html).

## How to edit the diagrams

- One diagram per case type.
- Node ids are the Java enum constants.
- An arrow label is the event id. A value in brackets is the field that selects that outcome, for example `applyWarrantAuthorisation [active]`.
- An arrow that leaves the outer box is legal from every state inside it.
- Draw a self-loop only when the handler returns that same state on purpose.
- Leave `setCaseState` off the diagram. It is a system-only prototype event that sets a PCN to any `CaseState` (`bin/set-case-state.sh`).
- Leave events that do not change state off the diagram. Record them in the tables below.

