Events that keep the current PCN state:

| Event | Allowed states | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `validateOotApplication` | `PENDING_CASE_ISSUED`, `CASE_ISSUED` | Clerk Next step |
| `editTe9Application` | all | Clerk Next step when `applicationForm` is `TE9` |
| `editPe3Application` | all | Clerk Next step when `applicationForm` is `PE3` |
| `editTe7Application` | all | Clerk Next step when `timeExtensionForm` is `TE7` |
| `editPe2Application` | all | Clerk Next step when `timeExtensionForm` is `PE2` |
| `recordApplication` | all | System, hidden |
| `recordTimeExtension` | all | System, hidden |
| `attachCaseFileDocument` | all | System, hidden |

## TEC_BATCH

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING: createBatch
    [*] --> QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING: uploadBatch
    QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING --> PROCESSING_STARTED: startBatchProcessing
    PROCESSING_STARTED --> PROCESSING_COMPLETE: completeBatchProcessing
    PROCESSING_STARTED --> PROCESSING_FAILED: failBatchProcessing
    PROCESSING_COMPLETE --> PROCESSING_COMPLETE: completeBatchProcessing
    PROCESSING_FAILED --> PROCESSING_FAILED: failBatchProcessing
```

`uploadBatch` is the clerk and local-authority create journey from ExUI primary navigation. `createBatch` is the hidden system create. Both start at `QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING`.

`attachBatchDocument` and `linkPcnCases` are allowed in every batch state and do not change it. A PCN is linked from the PCN side by `linkBatchCase`, then from the batch side by `linkPcnCases`.

## TEC_EXCEPTION

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> EXCEPTION_PENDING_REVIEW: createExceptionCase
```

`EXCEPTION_PENDING_REVIEW` is the only exception state. It belongs to `TEC_EXCEPTION`, not to the PCN `CaseState` catalogue. `rejectItem` and `editPcn` are clerk Next steps on that state and do not change it. Local authority has no access to this case type.
